WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Unit 2 starts with the
context the code depends on.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.825
Every Kerberos account has
one of four dispositions,

3
00:00:06.825 --> 00:00:11.131
and it's the application owner's
decision from Module 3, D N P three,

4
00:00:11.131 --> 00:00:15.762
which this chapter reads from Chapter
3's run, never from a second list.

5
00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:21.533
Replatform: to a G M S A or a D M S A,
converted here, with the new account's name,

6
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:25.738
the workload and its hosts
in one more reviewed file;

7
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:30.824
to a managed identity or an app
registration, Chapter 5 moves it.

8
00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:35.283
Keep: it stays, with an
end date no later than G 5,

9
00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:38.175
and an S P N owner if it has S P N's.

10
00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:43.779
Keep Kerberos: it stays on Kerberos with
the authorizing official's acceptance,

11
00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:48.025
an S P N owner, and an end date no
later than decision D oh eight's.

12
00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:51.887
Or retire, through the plan's
reviewed decommission process.

13
00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:56.750
The program adds rules of its own,
its design guidance, not Microsoft's.

14
00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:59.175
The disposition is Chapter 3's.

15
00:00:59.175 --> 00:01:03.840
Who may retrieve a managed password
is reviewed data: for a G M S A,

16
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.325
one domain local group of its
hosts, never a computer account.

17
00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:11.700
Every new account follows the
managed service account standard.

18
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.888
Every write carries its SailPoint
request and ServiceNow change.

19
00:01:15.888 --> 00:01:22.300
The pipeline's own G M S A sends what it
can, and a person sends the D M S A steps.

20
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.813
A D M S A migration runs thirty
days before it completes.

21
00:01:26.813 --> 00:01:29.887
Every account that stays
ends within its bound.

22
00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:34.136
And never delete: the old account is
disabled and moved to a holding O U,

23
00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:37.700
and a person deletes it through
the decommission ticket.
